    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d310">

                <pb facs="0433" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg321"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Schuyler to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-11-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 16, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1260.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence on the
                    proposed opium conference, and especially to my telegram of October 26, I have
                    the honor to inform you that I am now in receipt of a note (No. 68) from the
                    minister for foreign affairs, copies of which I inclose. The substance of this
                    note I sent you last night by cable.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montgomery
                    Schuyler.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d310-a1.xml" xpointer="d310-a1"/>
